; fas9_assoc_extended.scr - facit script of step 9.15 (F9.12 and F9.11): the associative framework's other action
; bodies, parameters, constraints, variables, dimension bodies and arrays, with the changes AutoCAD makes to them.
; Run it with
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_assoc_extended.scr
; It starts from AutoCAD's own acad.dwt (a new empty drawing) and uses plain AutoCAD commands, no LISP (the core has
; none). One drawing is built (every part in its own place, so a pick finds one object) and saved as `assoc_extended`;
; every change after it is made after an UNDO mark and taken back to it (a plain U would undo the SAVEAS).
;
; What is made, and the record types AutoCAD writes for it (2018, ASCII; the same in 2000 … 2018 and binary):
;   2D constraints   GCHORIZONTAL (2 points), DCLINEAR, DCANGULAR (3 points), GCCOINCIDENT, GCFIX, GCVERTICAL, DCVERTICAL,
;                    DCALIGNED, AUTOCONSTRAIN: ACDBASSOC2DCONSTRAINTGROUP, ACDBASSOCGEOMDEPENDENCY (the lines)
;   parameters       -PARAMETERS (a user parameter), a constraint whose value is an expression of it, a constraint
;                    value of a fraction: ACDBASSOCVARIABLE, ACDBASSOCVALUEDEPENDENCY
;   arrays           ARRAYRECT, ARRAYPOLAR, ARRAYPATH with ARRAYASSOCIATIVITY 1; ARRAYEDIT: ACDBASSOCARRAYACTIONBODY and
;                    (a replaced item) ACDBASSOCARRAYMODIFYACTIONBODY
;   surfaces         SURFOFFSET (ACDBASSOCOFFSETSURFACEACTIONBODY, ACDBASSOCASMBODYACTIONPARAM), SURFEXTEND, SURFBLEND,
;                    SURFPATCH, SURFNETWORK, SURFTRIM (ACDBASSOCTRIMSURFACEACTIONBODY, ACDBASSOCTRIMMINGPATHACTIONPARAM,
;                    ACDBASSOCRESTOREENTITYSTATEACTIONBODY), SURFFILLET (ACDBASSOCFILLETSURFACEACTIONBODY,
;                    ACDBASSOCFACEACTIONPARAM), FILLETEDGE and CHAMFEREDGE of a surface
;                    (ACDBASSOCEDGEFILLETACTIONBODY, ACDBASSOCEDGECHAMFERACTIONBODY)
;   dimensions       DIMASSOC 2 with DIMLINEAR, DIMALIGNED, DIMANGULAR, DIMORDINATE, DIMDIAMETER, DIMRADIUS on the vertices
;                    and circle edges of a solid (SOLIDHIST 1): ACDBASSOCROTATEDDIMACTIONBODY, ...ALIGNEDDIM...,
;                    ...3POINTANGULARDIM..., ...ORDINATEDIM..., ...DIAMETRICDIM..., ...RADIALDIM...,
;                    ACDBASSOCOSNAPPOINTREFACTIONPARAM, ACDBASSOCVERTEXACTIONPARAM
;   MLEADER          attached to a solid's vertex: ACDBASSOCMLEADERACTIONBODY
;   solids           a box and a cylinder with FILLETEDGE and CHAMFEREDGE: the persistent subentity managers with history
;
; Changes: -PARAMETERS Edit (a user parameter, a dimension's value), ARRAYEDIT (rows, a replaced item), a MOVE of the
; geometry, and an ERASE of what an action depends on (the profile, a cutting curve, an array's source, a constrained
; line, a solid): AutoCAD erases the actions that depended on it (plan, F9.12; HDxf does the same, B19).
;
; What AutoCAD 2025's core cannot do, and what is therefore "ej testat" (plan 2026-10-27-fas-9-typer.md, F9.12):
;   - ACDBASSOCCOMPOUNDACTIONPARAM, ACDBASSOCOBJECTACTIONPARAM, ACDBASSOCDIMDEPENDENCYBODY and
;     ACDBASSOCENTITYCLONEACTIONBODY: no command of the core makes one (searched: the commands of this script, the ones
;     of fas9_assoc_core.scr and the 111 sample drawings AutoCAD 2025 installs)
;   - selecting an array item with a pick (Ctrl-click) to move it: only ARRAYEDIT's REPlace makes an item override
;   - a constraint made by picking an object (GCPARALLEL, GCPERPENDICULAR, GCTANGENT ...): a typed point is no pick
;     for those commands; AUTOCONSTRAIN applies what a window of objects asks for
